==== Notes ====
  - On version 1.0 of this device, OpenWrt can be loaded from the router's standard firmware upgrade page. To be safe, use the relevant openwrt-xx.xx.x-ipq806x-generic-tplink_c2600-squashfs-factory.bin, then after initial installation, use the openwrt-xx.xx.x-ipq806x-generic-tplink_c2600-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin and deselect to keep settings. Verified 2020/12/19 by Rygle on device version 1.0 from factory software Build 20150610 Rel. 32140 to OpenWrt 19.07.5 without any issues.
  - On Version 1.1 of this device, the factory default username and password doesn't work. Hence the need to use TFTP to load OpenWrt.
  - Some units with "v1.1" physical label are recognized in software as "v1.0". Installing OpenWrt by uploading the factory image via the standard firmware upgrade page works for these models. (2022/03 using OpenWrt 21.02.2)
  - Reset to admin/admin reported working if reset button held down while switching on the device
//I can confirm points 3 and 4. My device has a phisical label v1.1, but with TP-Link firmware 2017-03-06 it showed v1.0 on the admin page. So I reset the admin user's password to admin, then using the standard firmware upgrade page I installed ''openwrt-22.03.6-ipq806x-generic-tplink_c2600-squashfs-factory.bin'' without a problem.//

