==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====

->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp]]

=== Specific values needed for tftp ===
Press and hold the reset button. Then turn on the device.  Continue to hold the reset button for 15 seconds or until TFTP transfer occurs:

^ Bootloader tftp client IPv4 address  | 192.168.0.86   |
^ Bootloader MAC address (special)     | No special MAC address required   |
^ Firmware TFTP image                  | [[toh:tp-link:archer_c2600_v1#installation|Latest OpenWRT Factory Image (NOT sysupgrade)]] (**''NOTE:''** Change filename to //"ArcherC2600_1.0_tp_recovery.bin"//) |
^ TFTP transfer window                 | Approximately 5 seconds or less     |
^ TFTP window start                    | Approximately 5-10 seconds after power on   |
^ TFTP server IP address      | Set PC to static IPv4 192.168.0.66, subnet mask 255.255.255.0, as this is where the router looks for the TFTP server.       |
^ LAN Port to connect         |LAN 1 works, probably any of LAN ports 1-4.|

**Note:** Make sure the router and the PC are connected directly, not through a switch ([[https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?pid=331036#p331036|more info]])

===== Upgrading OpenWrt =====
->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.sysupgrade]]

==== LuCI Web Upgrade Process ====

  * Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1/cgi-bin/luci/admin/system/flash/%%'' LuCI Upgrade URL
  * Upload image file for sysupgrade to LuCI
  * Wait for reboot

==== Terminal Upgrade Process ====

If you don't have a GUI (LuCI) available, you can alternatively upgrade via the command line.
There are command line method for upgrading:

  * ''sysupgrade''

Note: It is important that you put the firmware image into the ramdisk (/tmp) before you start flashing.

=== sysupgrade ===

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1, then enter the following commands:

<code>
cd /tmp
wget http://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/trunk/XXX/xxx.abc
sysupgrade /tmp/xxx.abc
</code>


===== Debricking =====
-> [[docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:generic.debrick]]

If you are experimenting with C2600 and you flash the wrong firmware and the device doesn't boot, you can restore the factory firmware:
  * Set PC to fixed ip address 192.168.0.66, default gateway to 192.168.0.1, and netmask to 255.255.255.0
  * Download factory firmware from TP-Link and rename it to ''ArcherC2600_1.0_tp_recovery.bin''
  * Start a tftp server with the file ''ArcherC2600_1.0_tp_recovery.bin'' in its root directory
  * Turn off the router
  * Press and hold Reset button
  * Turn on router with the reset button pressed and wait ~15 seconds
  * Release the reset button and after a short time the firmware should be transferred from the tftp server
  * Wait ~5 minute to complete recovery.


