==== Sporadic Reboots ====
:!: In case of sporadic reboots it might help to add the following to "System" --> "Startup" --> "Local Startup" (e.g. ''/etc/rc.local'') (Sources: [[flyspray>3099]], [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/unexplained-hangs-freezes-and-reboots-with-archer-c2600/61999/17|Forum]]):
<code>
echo performance > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_governor
echo performance > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/cpufreq/scaling_governor
echo 1200000 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_max_freq
echo 1200000 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_min_freq
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpuidle/state0/disable
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpuidle/state1/disable
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/cpuidle/state0/disable
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/cpuidle/state1/disable
</code>

==== Alternative WiFi Module and Firmware ====
Per default the device uses wireless firmware and kernel module by [[https://www.candelatech.com/ath10k.php|Candela Technologies]]. In [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/tp-link-archer-c2600-running-poorly-from-21-02-and-onwards/117581|some cases, where WiFi does not perform as expected]], the driver can be swapped to the non-candelatech alternative. The non-candelatech driver contains [[https://media.ccc.de/v/32c3-7375-wireless_drivers_freedom_considered_harmful/|mainly close-source-software with drawbacks]].
<code>
opkg update && opkg remove ath10k-firmware-qca99x0-ct kmod-ath10k-ct && opkg install ath10k-firmware-qca99x0 kmod-ath10k
</code>
Instead of switching to the closed-source driver a variant of the candelatech driver can be tried first (firmware remains the -ct type):
<code>
opkg update && opkg remove kmod-ath10k-ct && opkg install kmod-ath10k-ct-smallbuffers
</code>
To go back to the default drivers:
<code>
opkg update && opkg remove ath10k-firmware-qca99x0 kmod-ath10k kmod-ath10k-ct-smallbuffers
opkg update && opkg install ath10k-firmware-qca99x0-ct kmod-ath10k-ct
</code>

